    Clerk: Act 21 s4 requires a 'most recent restart' timestamp that nothing records
    
    The Act's own words make the boundary a recorded artifact and P2 depends on it, but no such record
    exists anywhere - government-setup.last advances within a run, so it is not a restart stamp, and
    boot.sh writes none. The ordinary operating cycle is therefore uncomputable and the s4 deadline
    unmeasurable. No breach today: main is green.
    
    Handed to the Executive with an exact recorder spec (boot_id from /proc, started_at only on boot_id
    change) and four acceptance criteria. Not a bill: s4 already requires the record.

